  "result": "**What it does:** Order utilities for a shop backend — `calcTotal` sums item price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies SAVE10/SAVE20 codes, `averageItemPrice` computes the mean, `formatOrder` renders a receipt string.\n\n**Bugs:**\n- `orders.js:5` — off-by-one: `i <= items.length` reads past the end; `items[items.length]` is `undefined`, so `.price` throws `TypeError`. Use `i < items.length`.\n- `orders.js:20` — `averageItemPrice` divides by `items.length` with no guard; empty array returns `NaN` (also 0/0). Guard for empty.\n- Minor: `averageItemPrice` averages the *discountable* total but ignores discounts, while `formatOrder` applies them — inconsistent, likely fine by design but worth confirming.",
